 in this timeline  there was a lot of interesting stuff in  the opening montage  and there are a bunch of short videos  included on the watch page on apple tv  that fill in more details about the  years that have passed between  seasons some of the most important  things that jumped out to me  in relation to the show's timeline is  that ronald reagan became president in  1976  instead of 1980 and at that same time  the space treaty with the soviet  union was scrapped this means that  reagan is coming to the end of his  second term  and that there is the possibility of  militarizing things on the moon  nasa has successfully landed an unmanned  rover on mars  after several failed attempts by both  the us and the soviets  perhaps because of the continued focus  on the space race  the soviets never invaded afghanistan  and in our timeline that was a  contributing factor  in their fall they never really fully  recovered from that the us involvement  there  in operation cyclone which funded the  mujahideen  also led to the rise of terrorist  organizations in that region  and produced characters like osama bin  laden so there's some interesting ripple  effects there for how  both sides will progress over the next  few decades  and to this point nothing has happened  to slow down the space race  the us now has a fleet of nasa space  shuttles and the military  has shuttles of their own there's a next  generation shuttle called the pathfinder  already in the works and we see that  some of the technology developed for the  space program  is producing advancements in everyday  life there are electric cars now with  these cool remote controls  and three mile island never happened i  guess the thing that seems most  important for our story  is that we get the feeling that tensions  in the cold war are very high  we hear bradford mention berlin to  margot and in the video  short about 1982 we find out that there  was an incident there  at that time where a couple escaped over  the berlin wall  they were pursued by an east german tank  and killed on the other side and that  led to a situation where  the two sides exchanged fire that raised  the threat level to defcon 4  and later in the episode when the solar  storm happens  we see bradford make the recommendation  to move to deathcon  3. the solar storm is the big event of  the  episode we go back to the moon where  everything was gonna be all right  and learn that actually it's not a solar  flare event on the sun produces a  coronal mass ejection  which basically means a cloud of  radiation is moving fast away from the  sun  everything outside of earth's atmosphere  is at risk of exposure to a high dose of  radiation  on the moon all of the astronauts are  able to make it to shelter  except molly cobb and the dutch  astronaut wubbo  he crashes his rover on the way to  safety and molly has to make a decision  on whether or not to go after him  first of all this sequence looked  fantastic the regolith on the surface  lifting up  combined with the score really gave it  an intense feeling and while it seems  like going out into the radiation was a  mistake  it does track with what we know about  this character  dumb thing to do but exactly what you  would expect to see from molly  because she removed her dissimilar we  don't know for sure  how bad her exposure was but based on  what margot described we have to imagine  that she'll likely get cancer in the  future  it's not clear if she was able to save  wubbo but if she did  it's likely the last heroic move she'll  be able to make as an astronaut  and that's a good transition into where  we think things are going i think the  cold war stuff and the season 2 trailer  are certainly hinting towards a  potential armed conflict on the moon  not much in this episode to see how  that'll be set in motion though  i think ed looked pretty confident in  his role as head of astronauts but have  a suspicion we'll see him put himself on  the roster of an upcoming  mission just like deke put himself on  one back in season one  the idea of karen running her own  business seems like a way for her to  refocus  but she's such a strong character i feel  like she'll be doing more than just  upgrading the parmesan  speaking of that it feels like if the  show is jumping a decade each season  then it's set up for the conflict that  surrounds the transition  from the old school to the new  generation ed's wanting that  old cheap shaker cheese he's used to  felt like some foreshadowing to me gordo  putting on weight and blatantly getting  drunk  even ordering another scotch from the  podium while he's speaking  looks like a setup for him to try to  make a comeback it wasn't clear how much  tracy was involved with nasa at this  moment  in this episode but based on the promo  materials  it looks like she'll be heading back to  space during this season as well  margot seems like the rock still so  it'll be interesting to see what gets in  her way this season molly probably won't  die  at least not right away i have to guess  that she'll be done as an active  astronaut though  she's also a great character so let's  hope they find something for her to do  that keeps her involved with things  i thought this was a really promising  start season one had some great ideas  and some memorable events  and i never thought about not continuing  when i was watching it but it sort of  had too much going on and it just felt  weighed down and unsatisfying in a lot  of places  at the same time the space stuff all  looked great it's cool to speculate on  the idea they're putting out there  how things would change the cast is  solid all the way down  the score is top-notch and put together  they pull  off some powerful moments what's  promising about season 2  is that the world is already established  and perhaps that'll mean the end of some  of the slogginess  the beginning of the second season comes  off as a big improvement and i'm excited  to see 